# 🌌 Anti-Gravity Digital Universe — Elite Implementation Plan

> **Goal:** Refactor Ameen's personal portfolio to compete for an **Awwwards SOTD**.  
> **Vibe:** *Mad Scientist meets Minimalist Designer*

---

## Executive Summary

Transform the current Vite + Vue 3 SPA portfolio into a **Nuxt 3-powered immersive 3D experience** with a persistent WebGL canvas, 1M+ particle systems, physics-based interactions, custom GLSL shaders, and a camera rig that moves through a 3D spline path controlled by scroll. The result: a portfolio that feels like stepping into a living, breathing digital universe.

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Current State<br/>Vite + Vue 3 SPA<br/>GSAP + ScrollTrigger<br/>Flat 2D Layout"] --> B["Target State<br/>Nuxt 3 + TresJS<br/>Full WebGL Pipeline<br/>Anti-Gravity 3D Universe"]
    style A fill:#333,color:#fff,stroke:#666
    style B fill:#0d1117,color:#7ee787,stroke:#7ee787
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Framework Migration Decision**: This plan proposes migrating from **Vite + Vue 3** to **Nuxt 3**. While Nuxt provides SSR/SSG for SEO (critical for a portfolio), it adds hydration complexity with GSAP/WebGL. **Alternative**: Stay on Vite + Vue 3 SPA and use prerendering for SEO. This is simpler but sacrifices some SEO features.

> [!WARNING]
> **Scope & Timeline**: This is an enormous undertaking. The full plan as described would take a senior creative developer **4-8 weeks** of focused work. I recommend a **phased delivery** where each phase produces a deployable, impressive result. We should decide together which phases to tackle first.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Mobile Performance**: FBO particle systems and GLSL shaders are GPU-intensive. The plan includes a "graceful degradation" strategy for mobile, but this means mobile users will experience a simpler (though still beautiful) version of the site.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Nuxt 3 Application Layer"
        N[Nuxt 3 App] --> R[Router / Pages]
        N --> P[Pinia Store]
        P --> |"Shared WebGL State<br/>Camera, Scroll %, Scene Mode"| WS[WebGL State Store]
        P --> |"UI State<br/>Active Section, Menu"| US[UI State Store]
    end

    subgraph "Persistent WebGL Layer (TresJS)"
        WS --> TC["TresCanvas<br/>(Full-viewport, persistent)"]
        TC --> SC[Scene Controller]
        SC --> PS["FBO Particle System<br/>(1M particles)"]
        SC --> GEO["Generative Geometry<br/>(Morphing Objects)"]
        SC --> CR["Camera Rig<br/>(Spline Path)"]
        SC --> PP["Post-Processing<br/>(Bloom, ChromAb, Grain)"]
    end

    subgraph "GSAP Orchestration Layer"
        R --> |"Route Changes"| GO[GSAP Observer]
        GO --> |"Scroll Progress"| WS
        ST[ScrollTrigger] --> |"Section Triggers"| SC
        TL[Master Timeline] --> |"Sequence Control"| SC
    end

    subgraph "HTML Content Layer"
        R --> HS[Hero Section]
        R --> AS[About Section]
        R --> FP[Featured Projects]
        R --> CS[Contact Section]
    end

    style TC fill:#1a1a2e,color:#e94560,stroke:#e94560
    style PS fill:#1a1a2e,color:#0f3460,stroke:#0f3460
    style CR fill:#1a1a2e,color:#16213e,stroke:#16213e
```

