## Proposed Changes

### Phase 0: Foundation — Nuxt 3 Migration & Shared Canvas

This phase establishes the architectural skeleton. Everything else builds on this.

---

#### Nuxt 3 Project Setup

##### [NEW] `nuxt.config.ts`
Nuxt 3 configuration with TresJS module, GSAP (via Nuxt plugin), Tailwind CSS v4, and custom font loading. Key settings:
- `ssr: true` with `routeRules` for static generation (SSG) of all portfolio pages
- TresJS module registered
- GSAP registered as a client-only plugin
- Custom `app.head` meta tags (preserve existing SEO)

##### [NEW] `plugins/gsap.client.ts`
Client-only Nuxt plugin that registers all GSAP plugins globally:
- `ScrollTrigger`, `ScrollSmoother`, `Observer`, `Flip`, `Draggable`, `CustomEase`
- Provides `$gsap` via `nuxtApp.provide()` for use in composables

##### [NEW] `plugins/tres.client.ts`
Client-only plugin for TresJS initialization and any global Three.js configuration.

---

#### Shared WebGL Canvas (The "Continuous Rendering" Architecture)

##### [NEW] `stores/webgl.ts` (Pinia)
The brain of the 3D experience. Manages:
```typescript
interface WebGLState {
  scrollProgress: number        // 0-1 global scroll %
  activeSection: string         // 'hero' | 'about' | 'projects' | 'contact'
  cameraTarget: Vector3         // Where the camera should look
  cameraPosition: Vector3       // Where the camera is
  particleMode: string          // 'idle' | 'explode' | 'attract' | 'morph'
  mousePosition: { x: number, y: number }
  isTransitioning: boolean
  scrollVelocity: number        // For post-processing intensity
  audioReactivity: number       // 0-1 from audio analyzer
}
```

##### [NEW] `components/WebGLCanvas.vue`
- A **full-viewport `<TresCanvas>`** positioned `fixed` behind all HTML content
- Placed in `app.vue` (NOT inside pages) so it persists across route changes
- Contains the Scene Controller, Camera Rig, Particle System, Post-Processing
- Watches the Pinia store reactively to update 3D scene

##### [MODIFY] `app.vue`
```vue
<template>
  <!-- Persistent 3D Layer (never unmounts) -->
  <ClientOnly>
    <WebGLCanvas />
  </ClientOnly>
  
  <!-- HTML Content Layer (scrollable, transparent bg) -->
  <div class="content-layer">
    <NuxtPage />
  </div>
</template>
```

