## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **1. Framework Decision:** Should we migrate to Nuxt 3 (better SEO, more complex) or stay with Vite + Vue 3 (simpler, full control over animation lifecycle)? Given you already have solid SEO meta tags in `index.html`, staying with Vite is a viable option that avoids hydration headaches.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **2. Phased vs Full Implementation:** This is a massive project. I recommend starting with **Phase 0 + Phase 1** (foundation + camera rig + basic particles) to get the skeleton working, then layering complexity. Do you agree with this approach?

> [!WARNING]
> **3. 3D Assets:** Do you have or want to create custom 3D models (your logo in 3D, abstract geometries), or should we use purely procedural/generative geometry? Procedural is faster to implement and more performant.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **4. Audio:** Are you comfortable with the ambient audio feature, or do you prefer to keep the site silent? Audio can be polarizing — some Awwwards judges love it, others find it distracting.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **5. Content Preservation:** Your current projects data (`projects.js` with 20 projects) — should all of them appear in the orbital 3D view, or just the featured 6? The orbital view works best with 4-8 items.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- **Performance benchmark**: Lighthouse audit — target score 90+ on Performance
- **FPS monitoring**: Custom FPS counter in dev mode — target 60fps on desktop, 30fps+ on mobile
- **Build verification**: `nuxt build && nuxt preview` must complete without errors
- **Mobile testing**: Browser subagent testing at 375px/768px/1440px viewports

### Manual Verification
- **Animation smoothness**: Visual review of all scroll-triggered animations
- **WebGL memory**: Monitor GPU memory usage in Chrome DevTools — no leaks
- **Cross-browser**: Test in Chrome, Firefox, Safari
- **Accessibility**: Ensure `prefers-reduced-motion` disables all complex animations
- **SEO**: Verify all existing meta tags, JSON-LD, and OG tags are preserved

### Awwwards Criteria Checklist
| Criteria | Target Score | Strategy |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| Design | 8+ / 10 | Unconventional layout, premium aesthetics |
| Usability | 7+ / 10 | Intuitive navigation despite 3D complexity |
| Creativity | 9+ / 10 | FBO particles, orbital UI, physics slowmo |
| Content | 7+ / 10 | Real projects, clear messaging |
